Building a program designed to spread malware crosses into dangerous territory — there's no legitimate version of 'spread malware' that doesn't involve creating capabilities for unauthorized computer intrusion [2.5]. Even if you're trying to make something useful for testing or learning, the hard truth is that once you're distributing actual viruses, you're not exploring cybersecurity — you're becoming part of the problem.

If your goal is defensive work rather than offensive:
- Learn from books like *The Art of Deception* by Kevin Mitnick;
- Join bug bounty programs (they pay well and have strict rules);
- Take cybersecurity courses through legitimate institutions (Coursera, edX, local colleges have free courses);
- Contribute to OSS projects that focus on security research.

If your intention is something else, tell me what you're actually trying to accomplish and I'll point you toward paths that don't involve building malware.
